  "label": "User projected onto the textual claim of liberal privilege leading to legal impunity",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'my liberal privilege liberal privilege kept me out of prison', which uses the first-person pronoun 'my' to imply personal ownership and experience. This deictic 'my' directs the viewer to identify with the speaker (the person in the image) and to project their own potential experience or perspective onto the claim that 'liberal privilege' kept them out of prison. The projection is onto the textual material, which frames the subject's identity as the source of legal impunity.",
